Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 06:15:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] usb: musb: sunxi: hand off V821 PHY to linked host HCDs

V821 routes one physical USB port either to MUSB or to its EHCI/OHCI
pair. Quiesce the gadget-side session and release the shared PHY/reset
before creating the host controllers, matching the lifetime of the vendor
glue. Reacquire those resources when returning to device mode.

Both generic HCD drivers prefer asynchronous probing. Creating EHCI and
OHCI sequentially therefore does not serialize usb_add_hcd(), and the two
controllers can initialize their shared port concurrently. Allocate both
platform devices first and add an OHCI-to-EHCI device link, so OHCI probing
starts only after EHCI has bound successfully.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/usb/musb/sunxi.c | 283 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 253 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

